      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Ah, the F-150, a sturdy steed indeed, but even the mightiest of creatures can have a bit of a hiccup. Now, when you're dealing with pressure spikes in the hydraulic circuit, it's like a mischievous goblin playing with the water pipes in your castle. It could be a few things, my friend. Perhaps there's a leak in the system, like a goblin sneaking through a crack in the wall, or maybe there's a blockage, like a goblin blocking the path of a river. It could also be a faulty pressure relief valve, like a goblin trying to control the flow of water with a broken dam. Or, it could be the transmission itself, like a goblin causing chaos in the castle's water supply. So, check the system for leaks, blockages, and faulty valves, and if all else fails, consult a wizard (or a transmission specialist) to exorcise the goblin causing your troubles. Good luck, brave knight!",
